dirty flag is set to `DIRTY_EULER_ROTATION_AND_SCALE`. And in the subsequent `get_basis()` or `get_transform()` call, `_test_dirty_bits(DIRTY_LOCAL_TRANSFORM)` set the flag to `DIRTY_LOCAL_TRANSFORM & DIRTY_EULER_ROTATION_AND_SCALE` (which is 0) and returned `DIRTY_EULER_ROTATION_AND_SCALE` (which, when converted to boolean, is true). This caused transform to be unexpectedly re-derived from euler angles and scale, while the intended behavior is clearly \"mark euler angle and scale as dirty and use transform as the source of truth\". It really should have returned `DIRTY_LOCAL_TRANSFORM & DIRTY_EULER_ROTATION_AND_SCALE`.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3865934965/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3873929247","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116012#issuecomment-3873929247","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116012","id":3873929247,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7m53gf","user":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","r